Two files below. The earlier build trapped because `panic!` fired when the store returned nothing under `"urls"`, and `panic = "abort"` turns that into an `unreachable` trap. The body now never panics. It tries a few likely keys and accepts either a JSON array or a plain list of URLs. If nothing is found, it returns an empty list instead of trapping. I could not tell from the contract whether `present(urls)` requires a non-empty list. I chose not to invent URLs, so if the store holds nothing, that case would still fail the contract check.

